# Week 1 – Introduction to DevOps and Git/GitHub

## Objective

The objective of this week is to understand the basic concepts of DevOps and learn the fundamentals of Git and GitHub.

## Tasks

### Task 1: Introduction to DevOps

* Understand the concept of DevOps.
* Learn the importance of DevOps in software development.
* Understand the DevOps lifecycle.
* Learn about Continuous Integration (CI) and Continuous Deployment (CD).

### Task 2: Install and Configure Git

* Install Git on the system.
* Configure username and email.
* Verify the Git installation.

### Task 3: Create GitHub Repository

* Create a new repository on GitHub.
* Create folders for weekly tasks.
* Add a README file to the repository.

### Task 4: Perform Basic Git Commands

The following Git commands were practiced:

```bash
git --version
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"
git init
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git log
git remote -v
git push
```

